<title>UK: Energy trades well below PacifiCorp offer.</title>
<headline>Energy trades well below PacifiCorp offer.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Energy Group Plc traded on Friday at a larger discount to PacifiCorp's offer price than other bid-target utilities in the past, analysts said.</p>
<p>Energy Group was 1/2p higher at 648-1/2p, a seven percent discount to the 6.955 stg-a-share offer.</p>
<p>&quot;There's much more uncertainty over this deal with a new and untried Labour government and the possibility of a windfall tax,&quot; said one analyst.</p>
<p>Others have traded at discounts of near five percent, analysts said.  </p>
<p>More than six million shares changed hands by 0933 GMT making it the fifth most actively traded stock in the London market.</p>
<p>-- Louise Ireland, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
